WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.181 --> 00:00:02.149
I always thought that maybe a wedding

00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:04.400
would be the incentive
I needed to lose weight,

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.198
so when I got engaged, I decided
to start looking into it.

00:00:08.198 --> 00:00:10.980
But after I did a little
research, it quickly became clear

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.277
that the best diet was
actually no diet at all

00:00:14.277 --> 00:00:17.571
because it turns out, dieting
can make you gain weight.

00:00:17.571 --> 00:00:20.579
(upbeat music)

00:00:20.579 --> 00:00:22.509
Yeah, diets have been
around for hundreds of years

00:00:22.509 --> 00:00:24.549
and so you might think,
well, it's time tested,

00:00:24.549 --> 00:00:26.438
hundreds of years, we gotta trust it.

00:00:26.438 --> 00:00:29.360
But you would be wrong,
you'd be very wrong.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.918
So here's the science behind why

00:00:30.918 --> 00:00:32.909
dieting can make you gain weight.

00:00:32.909 --> 00:00:34.661
Body weight is regulated by the brain,

00:00:34.661 --> 00:00:37.229
and which is often resistant
to extreme diet-based

00:00:37.229 --> 00:00:39.451
weight loss, so when you're on a diet,

00:00:39.451 --> 00:00:41.301
sure, initially you might lose weight,

00:00:41.301 --> 00:00:42.987
but likely you're gonna gain it back

00:00:42.987 --> 00:00:45.731
because your body's gonna make you.

00:00:45.731 --> 00:00:47.619
The hormone leptin plays an important

00:00:47.619 --> 00:00:49.198
role in our eating habits.

00:00:49.198 --> 00:00:50.819
This hormone combats our attempts

00:00:50.819 --> 00:00:53.180
at weight loss by signaling hunger.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:56.692
Basically, you scared your
body because you starved it,

00:00:56.692 --> 00:00:59.453
and so your body is like, okay, bitch,

00:00:59.453 --> 00:01:01.981
I'm gonna start storin'
up fat, so if you do this

00:01:01.981 --> 00:01:04.632
to me again, I'm gonna
have some fat storage

00:01:04.632 --> 00:01:06.701
to be able to deal with that starvation.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:09.043
This is the called the
classic starvation response.

00:01:09.043 --> 00:01:11.683
The brain responds to a
loss of fat by increasing

00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:13.741
your hunger levels, so
now you're more hungry,

00:01:13.741 --> 00:01:15.971
and you may eat more food,
so if you're dieting,

00:01:15.971 --> 00:01:18.461
you are far more
vulnerable to binge eating.

00:01:18.461 --> 00:01:21.432
Dieting can be stressful in
itself, and stress hormones

00:01:21.432 --> 00:01:25.061
are linked to weight gain,
especially in the belly area.

00:01:25.061 --> 00:01:27.363
Just so you can understand
how silly diets are,

00:01:27.363 --> 00:01:29.141
I think it's best to look back

00:01:29.141 --> 00:01:31.363
on the dieting fads of yesteryear.

00:01:31.363 --> 00:01:33.180
The creator of graham crackers introduced

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.699
a high fiber diet in the 1830s.

00:01:35.699 --> 00:01:37.027
We all know what happened, obviously,

00:01:37.027 --> 00:01:39.345
camping became big, we
started eating s'mores.

00:01:39.345 --> 00:01:41.318
Graham crackers aren't that
healthy when you put chocolate

00:01:41.318 --> 00:01:44.947
and marshmallow on them,
but they are delicious.

00:01:44.947 --> 00:01:48.238
There was William Banting's
low-carb diet from 1863.

00:01:48.238 --> 00:01:50.867
In 1903, it was popular
for people to chew food

00:01:50.867 --> 00:01:54.108
32 times in order to lose weight

00:01:54.108 --> 00:01:57.007
and digest food better, I guess?

00:01:57.007 --> 00:01:58.478
There's a lot more things you could do

00:01:58.478 --> 00:02:01.519
to lose those calories than
just sittin' and chewin'.

00:02:01.519 --> 00:02:04.261
The cigarette diet debuted in 1925,

00:02:04.261 --> 00:02:06.440
and we all know how that went.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.929
Yeah, cigarettes, not so healthy.

00:02:08.929 --> 00:02:11.561
The grapefruit diet debuted in 1930,

00:02:11.561 --> 00:02:13.481
and it was popularized in Hollywood.

00:02:13.481 --> 00:02:15.561
The idea behind the grapefruit
diet was that if you eat

00:02:15.561 --> 00:02:17.751
a grapefruit with every meal,
you're gonna lose weight.

00:02:17.751 --> 00:02:19.711
I mean, I love grapefruits but

00:02:19.711 --> 00:02:21.881
does anyone love grapefruit that much?

00:02:21.881 --> 00:02:24.039
A grapefruit every meal,
that's too much grapefruit.

00:02:24.039 --> 00:02:26.519
In 1934, the United Fruit Company began

00:02:26.519 --> 00:02:28.988
pushing the banana and skim milk diet.

00:02:28.988 --> 00:02:30.748
So you see the pattern
here, people are trying

00:02:30.748 --> 00:02:32.729
to sell you things, and
they're trying to sell you it

00:02:32.729 --> 00:02:34.538
by telling you, you're
gonna lose weight with it.

00:02:34.538 --> 00:02:37.308
This is a pattern that
repeats throughout time.

00:02:37.308 --> 00:02:40.577
On the Sleeping Beauty
diet, which debuted in 1976,

00:02:40.577 --> 00:02:43.846
people were sedated for days
in order to lose weight.

00:02:43.846 --> 00:02:45.255
Like Sleeping Beauty had an excuse,

00:02:45.255 --> 00:02:47.806
there was a curse put on her,
but you just cursed yourself.

00:02:47.806 --> 00:02:50.785
Or maybe society cursed you into thinking

00:02:50.785 --> 00:02:55.195
you needed to lose weight by
doing the Sleeping Beauty diet.

00:02:55.195 --> 00:02:57.555
The caveman diet came out in 1985 and that

00:02:57.555 --> 00:03:00.122
has morphed into what we
know today as the Paleo diet,

00:03:00.122 --> 00:03:02.132
where you just eat a bunch
of meat for some reason.

00:03:02.132 --> 00:03:03.861
The trendy diets of today are the

00:03:03.861 --> 00:03:06.332
Whole30, Paleo Diet, and the Keto Diet.

00:03:06.332 --> 00:03:09.863
Christine Clark, PhD, RDN,
she cautions against diets

00:03:09.863 --> 00:03:11.863
that prohibit certain food groups, which,

00:03:11.863 --> 00:03:16.200
if you've ever tried a diet,
is like, most of all diets.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.292
Dieters who avoid specific food groups

00:03:18.292 --> 00:03:21.425
lose out in the nutrients
that are in those food groups.

00:03:21.425 --> 00:03:23.954
The Keto Diet is a
high-fat, low-carb diet,

00:03:23.954 --> 00:03:25.607
which could result in inadequate

00:03:25.607 --> 00:03:28.544
levels of antioxidants,
fiber, and vitamins.

00:03:28.544 --> 00:03:30.866
The Whole30 is an
extremely restrictive diet.

00:03:30.866 --> 00:03:35.033
You have to eliminate dairy,
beans, grains, sugar, alcohol.

00:03:35.894 --> 00:03:38.726
The diet's restrictiveness
can make it unsustainable.

00:03:38.726 --> 00:03:40.424
If you're dieting and you're following an

00:03:40.424 --> 00:03:44.525
unsustainable diet, you're
gonna fall back to bad habits.

00:03:44.525 --> 00:03:47.606
Our society is obsessed with
skinniness for no reason.

00:03:47.606 --> 00:03:50.504
Skinny's not always been
the ideal body type.

00:03:50.504 --> 00:03:52.694
Until the 1900s, curvy women were the

00:03:52.694 --> 00:03:55.155
ideal beauty standard
in the U.S. and Europe.

00:03:55.155 --> 00:03:57.294
There was singer/actress Lillian Russell,

00:03:57.294 --> 00:04:00.104
who would be considered
heavyset by today's standards.

00:04:00.104 --> 00:04:03.046
She was the ideal beauty
in the late 19th century.

00:04:03.046 --> 00:04:05.035
During the turn of the
century, the Gibson Girls

00:04:05.035 --> 00:04:06.926
set another body standard for women.

00:04:06.926 --> 00:04:09.474
The Gibson Girls were
simultaneously curvy and fragile.

00:04:09.474 --> 00:04:11.354
They had thin waists, thanks to corsets,

00:04:11.354 --> 00:04:14.634
and large breasts, so
that was also probably

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:18.243
a crazy body type to try to emulate.

00:04:18.243 --> 00:04:21.531
In the 1940s and 50s, advertisers
capitalized on the idea

00:04:21.531 --> 00:04:24.203
that women and who were skinny,
were unattractive to men.

00:04:24.203 --> 00:04:26.811
These are real ads that
were targeted at women

00:04:26.811 --> 00:04:28.704
to try to make them gain weight,

00:04:28.704 --> 00:04:31.933
which is just something that's
completely unheard of today.

00:04:31.933 --> 00:04:33.904
There were these ads
basically reinforced the idea

00:04:33.904 --> 00:04:36.501
that to find love, thin
women have to gain weight.

00:04:36.501 --> 00:04:38.592
After World War II and into the 1960s,

00:04:38.592 --> 00:04:41.053
we had Marilyn Monroe, who
had a very full figure,

00:04:41.053 --> 00:04:43.413
and was considered the
ideal beauty at the time.

00:04:43.413 --> 00:04:45.982
In the 1960s, that's when
thinness started to come

00:04:45.982 --> 00:04:49.184
into vogue, first with
Twiggy and Audrey Hepburn.

00:04:49.184 --> 00:04:52.282
Then in the 1990s, ultra-thin heroin chic

00:04:52.282 --> 00:04:55.352
was popularized by models like Kate Moss.

00:04:55.352 --> 00:04:58.064
Basically, beauty standards
change all the time,

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.504
and currently being a little skinny thing

00:05:00.504 --> 00:05:02.783
is very unrealistic for most people.

00:05:02.783 --> 00:05:05.893
You can be healthy when
you're slightly overweight,

00:05:05.893 --> 00:05:07.504
according to society's standards.

00:05:07.504 --> 00:05:10.243
You know what, [beep] all
these crazy fad diets.

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:13.824
Eat healthy, exercise, sleep,
watch your stress levels,

00:05:13.824 --> 00:05:16.203
and be happy in your body
'cuz your body's perfect

00:05:16.203 --> 00:05:18.732
the way it is, and honestly
trying to change it,

00:05:18.732 --> 00:05:20.784
might just be worse in the long run.

00:05:20.784 --> 00:05:23.367
(upbeat music)

